{
  "about": "The moves a line can make (Docs/Design/84 §7.2): what it does (a rule's `does`, a scene's per turn), what it makes due by default (expects; soft when optional), what it answers ('*': anything), what stands in when nothing doing it fits (fallback, down to ack), and how a dispreferred answer is shaped. An alias is an answer concept of the library's (settings.json) and the move its lines make: their commonest, until Phase 7 tags each line. A misspelt move, an `owes` naming a move that doesn't answer the line, or an unknown tone is refused when the library loads, and so is a dead end: a concept a line hands on to, or a move a line owes, with no plain line that holds when nothing is known.",
